00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:35.920
All right. Video game wise though, Indiana Jones and the temple of doom is another one of those unlicensed

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:42.420
then licensed Tenjin Atari games that they got like sued like crazy for by Nintendo.

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:45.620
You guys don't need me to recap this story anymore, right?

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:48.820
Um, I, I believe we've gone over it, right?

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:50.880
Yeah. No, three times now.

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:53.200
This is like, you know, RBI baseball had it.

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:55.700
Um, what was another one that had it?

00:06:55.940 --> 00:06:57.860
Uh, just did it.

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:01.580
We just did a big one on it, but a Pac-Man, Pac-Man had the problem.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:06.640
So Atari keeps trying to do this thing under a second company called Tenjin and it's just

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:07.460
not working out.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:12.400
And what's funny is, is we're finally playing temple of doom, but it took a long time to do

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:18.460
time for this version of the game to get to NES players because the film comes out in 84.

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:21.780
The arcade game comes out in 1985.

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:28.880
The arcade game is then ported to a bunch of other like computer systems in like 86.

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:37.160
Finally comes unlicensed to the, uh, NES by Tenjin in like early 1988.

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:40.020
And then everybody's like, no, no, no, you can't do that.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:47.360
So mindscape, another company releases the licensed version of temple of doom from Atari

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:49.180
in December of 88.

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:55.980
So, you know, from 84, 85 and 84, if you count the film all the way till now, it's been in

00:07:55.980 --> 00:08:00.460
the making, but it's like, finally you can play Indiana Jones and the temple of doom on

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:02.500
your NES. And I'm just not sure how many people were looking for that.

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:08.140
Yeah. It's actually so, so strange to think about because obviously like in the future there,

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:13.680
you know, the games would have released sometimes before the movie, like to, to capitalize on

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:16.960
the hype. Now it's just like, Oh, that was, that was four or five years ago.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:23.980
It's like a coordinated marketing strategy, uh, in like the nineties and the two thousands.

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:29.320
But, uh, yeah, this just seems like, like, Oh, what if, what if we made an Indiana Jones

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:32.380
game? Uh, I guess like a, I don't even know.

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:35.100
