00:09:02.820 --> 00:09:08.720
Yeah. They're just priming us right away on booting it up.

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:13.060
It's, it's on my shit list and I'm sure you can, you can understand why.

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:15.380
I'd like to hear it from you.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:19.820
Well, you start the game by pressing the start button.

00:09:19.940 --> 00:09:21.200
The game tells you that much.

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:26.880
It says push, push, start, you know, you push start the Indiana Jones music, which is

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:31.060
beautifully translated from, um, the score that we all know so well.

00:09:31.220 --> 00:09:34.100
It's now done, you know, really well on the NES.

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:38.920
Problem is, is that you push start to begin the music, but you don't actually start the

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:39.780
game. Yeah.

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:40.640
And then you press start again.

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:41.740
We are on the same page there.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:45.220
Yeah. You push start again and nothing happens.

00:09:45.500 --> 00:09:47.860
And then you're like, oh, it's one of those games where you press a instead.

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:50.540
And then you press a and nothing happens.

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:52.400
And then you start looking for the shoulder buttons.

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:54.020
