00:58:36.920 --> 00:58:46.580
But it just, yeah, the perspective, the controls, the repetitiveness in, in a, in a way that's not particularly fun because of the controls.

00:58:46.780 --> 00:58:53.440
Just all kind of adds together and makes it a not great experience when it could have been an okay experience.

00:58:53.440 --> 00:58:56.000
It had all that potential to be a decent experience.

00:58:56.840 --> 00:58:57.980
So I'm going to say no.

00:59:00.520 --> 00:59:02.400
I like how you're always hopeful, though.

00:59:02.960 --> 00:59:04.380
Sean, what do you got?

00:59:06.500 --> 00:59:14.080
This game has a lot of the complexity of the more recent games with, you know, like sort of a submenu sort of thing.

00:59:14.300 --> 00:59:20.600
And like, it seems to be going along the lines of than, than, than this would have been.

00:59:20.700 --> 00:59:29.320
But it's, it's design in terms of like the action, like the action design of this game is stuck in 1985.

00:59:29.820 --> 00:59:39.500
Like it, it does not feel good to play in any sense, aside from, I guess, when you're just walking to the left or right for Sam.

00:59:41.000 --> 00:59:43.160
I, I do not like this game.

00:59:43.360 --> 00:59:44.820
I am disappointed in this game.

00:59:45.140 --> 00:59:46.300
It is not essential.

00:59:47.960 --> 00:59:50.860
All right. So there's zero chance that's going to make it on the list.

00:59:51.000 --> 00:59:58.240
But I will add another vote against Indiana Jones and the Temple of Doom being on the essential games list.

00:59:58.240 --> 01:00:10.780
Because, you know, for me, the level layouts and the way that Indy controls, which is, if you think about it, 95% of the game is always, it always felt like a chore to me.

01:00:10.900 --> 01:00:13.940
It's actually not fun to do most of what they set out to do.

01:00:14.100 --> 01:00:22.400
But you, and I don't know if this is because we play these games for the show, but like I kept playing for a good while just because I was intrigued.

01:00:22.880 --> 01:00:27.380
I was intrigued by what they, what they positioned on the back of the box and on the manual.

01:00:27.680 --> 01:00:33.060
I was intrigued because I thought that it was laid out differently than the games were used to.

01:00:33.420 --> 01:00:41.020
Face it. If this game was just like a weird Indiana Jones shmup where you just kind of walk down a cave and you just whip at the enemies, right?

01:00:41.120 --> 01:00:43.080
Like as they come here on screen, that would be weird.

01:00:43.140 --> 01:00:44.240
And I'd be like, oh, I've seen that before.

01:00:44.240 --> 01:00:49.680
But we haven't really seen anything like this in terms of action adventure exploration.

01:00:50.020 --> 01:00:51.260
So I wanted to give it a try.

01:00:51.260 --> 01:00:53.080
I just never really liked it.

01:00:53.120 --> 01:00:54.500
So it can't go on the list.

01:00:55.220 --> 01:00:58.260
And it's not. You can rest easy tonight.

01:00:58.440 --> 01:01:02.960
